course: dictionary
lesson: 8450
title: A giant of the desert
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A saguaro is a giant cactus. It grows in the Sonoran Desert, in Arizona in the USA and in Mexico. You may not know the word, but the words around it give you clues about what it is.
explain: «The saguaro cactus of Arizona and Mexico can grow over 12 metres tall and live over 150 years.» A plant over 12 metres tall is taller than a house, and living over 150 years is very long for a plant. So a saguaro is huge and very old.
explain: «A cactus stores water in its stem and swells after rain.» Desert plants get little rain, so they need ways to keep water. The saguaro's stem works like a water store that swells when it fills up.
fact: A saguaro is a giant cactus that grows in the Sonoran Desert.
fact: The Sonoran Desert is in Arizona in the USA and in Mexico.
fact: A saguaro can grow taller than a house, and its arms point upwards.
fact: Its pleated stem swells to store water after rain.
fact: Its spines protect it, and woodpeckers and elf owls nest in holes in it.
exercise: «The saguaro cactus of Arizona and Mexico can grow over 12 metres tall.» How tall can a saguaro grow? | Only as tall as a pencil | *Over 12 metres | About 1 metre
exercise: Where does the saguaro grow? | *In the Sonoran Desert of Arizona, USA, and Mexico | In the Arctic snow | In the rainforests of Brazil | In the cold mountains of Norway
exercise: «Its spines are changed leaves that shade it and stop animals eating it.» Find and copy the word for the sharp parts that protect the cactus. | shade | arms | stem | *spines
test: «A cactus stores water in its stem and swells after rain.» Why does the stem swell? | *To store water after rain | To make the cactus lighter for the wind | To hide from birds
test: «The elf owl often nests in old woodpecker holes in saguaro cactuses.» Where does the elf owl nest? | On the bare sand | In a cave under the sea | *In old woodpecker holes in a saguaro
exam: «Its first arm often grows only at about 50 to 70 years old.» At about what age does a saguaro's first arm often grow? | 12 years | Under 5 years | *About 50 to 70 years
